          <section class="resume-group" id="internships">
            <h3 data-i18n="experience.internship"># Internship Experience</h3>
            <div class="resume-entry">
              <div class="resume-row"><time data-i18n="dates.nio">2026.09 — present</time><strong data-i18n="internship.nioTitle">NIO | AI Data Product Intern</strong></div>
              <ul class="internship-highlights">
                <li><h4 data-i18n="internship.nioPlatformTitle">Agent Operations Platform</h4><p data-i18n="internship.nioPlatform">Own the development and iteration of Shuling’s internal operations platform. Integrate query data across Agent versions and business domains, and design AI tagging to assess whether answers meet expectations. Daily Feishu cards bring operations, product, engineering and evaluation teams together to resolve high-priority issues, supporting Agent iteration with shared data and workflows.</p></li>
                <li><h4 data-i18n="internship.nioSkillsTitle">Agent System &amp; Domain Skills</h4><p data-i18n="internship.nioSkills">Clarify dashboard metric definitions against business needs and iterate Shuling’s system and domain Skills. Design evaluation criteria and datasets to improve answer quality and drive product adoption.</p></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="resume-entry">
              <div class="resume-row"><time>2026.01 — 2026.04</time><strong data-i18n="internship.poizonTitle">POIZON | AI Product Intern</strong></div>
              <ul class="internship-highlights">
                <li><h4 data-i18n="internship.poizonStrategyTitle">Intent Recognition &amp; Conversation Strategy</h4><p data-i18n="internship.poizonStrategy">Built scenario-based, multi-turn guidance for an AI shopping assistant. Defined four stages of user intent to guide follow-up questions, explanations, recommendations and conversion, addressing unfocused recommendations and incomplete shopping journeys. Raised AI adoption by 4.47% and product-card exposure by 44.85% (relative gains).</p></li>
                <li><h4 data-i18n="internship.poizonEvaluationTitle">Agent Tuning &amp; Evaluation</h4><p data-i18n="internship.poizonEvaluation">Independently designed four Agent personas and System Prompts, alongside an evaluation framework covering adoption, decision-making, interaction and recommendation. Increased overall AI adoption from 18.38% to 21.66%; decision-adoption UV and interaction-adoption UV improved by 3.38% and 1.50%, respectively (relative gains). Analyzed bad cases and user behavior to guide further iteration.</p></li>
                <li><h4 data-i18n="internship.poizonSkillsTitle">Reusable Skills for Data Analysis</h4><p data-i18n="internship.poizonSkills">Packaged data retrieval and analysis into reusable Skills for an internal Agent. Automated metric monitoring, change-point analysis and weekly reporting, saving each team member about 2.5 hours per week and improving routine analysis and experiment reviews.</p></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="resume-entry">
              <div class="resume-row"><time>2025.08 — 2025.11</time><strong data-i18n="internship.zhihuishuTitle">Zhihuishu.com | AI Product Intern</strong></div>
              <ul class="internship-highlights">
                <li><h4 data-i18n="internship.zhihuishuPipelineTitle">Multi-model Production &amp; Evaluation</h4><p data-i18n="internship.zhihuishuPipeline">Designed an automated medical knowledge-card pipeline and quality evaluation framework to address gaps in long-form generation and duplicate references. Coordinated models across parsing, generation, evidence verification and database ingestion, achieving a 97.8% ingestion acceptance rate. Analyzed 8,000+ bad cases and built an evaluation dataset based on the evidence-based medicine hierarchy to support production at scale.</p></li>
                <li><h4 data-i18n="internship.zhihuishuResearchTitle">User Research &amp; Product Prototyping</h4><p data-i18n="internship.zhihuishuResearch">Researched domestic and international competitors to clarify positioning, audiences, use cases and business models for an AI knowledge base. Developed product directions for education and professional knowledge services, and completed three web-prototype iterations across conversational and detail pages to inform feature planning and commercialization.</p></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </section>

